==Battleground==
*1 [[Mooth]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*1 [[Owlbrow]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Owlbrow]] spawns after 116.67 seconds<sup>3,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Mooth]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
**2 [[Teacher Bun Bun]]s spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
For early game players, attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] or [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] will greatly help in clearing this stage, though you will need [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] as meatshields to support them.

For late game players, to efficiently grind this stage you will need rushers such as [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to quickly blitz the stage and its threats, crowd-controlling units such as Octopus Cat can optionally be helpful in clearing the stage but are somewhat slow. Use [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] to protect your rushers while they wail on the base.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] that has a [[Special Abilities|special ability]] against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies should do well here. Their range doesn't have to be too high either, as the Bun Buns obstruct the Owlbrows from being able to hit your Ubers most of the time. Below are more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber]]: Her rapid [[Long Distance]] attacks combined with her [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies speeds this stage up a lot.
*[[Strike Unit R.E.I. (Uber Rare Cat)|Strike Unit R.E.I.]]: Same as Saber minus the Long Distance and rapid attacks (unless you have R.E.I.'s [[True Form]]), just make sure that another one of your units don't knockback the Bun Buns so R.E.I. won't miss her attack.
*[[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Catman]]: Long-ranged [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] against Floating enemies. Just like R.E.I., make sure he doesn't miss his attack.
*[[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]]: Fast [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] that can snipe the Owlbrows from behind the Bun Buns and give you an injection of cash, all while doing pretty big damage to them.
*[[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]]: Same as Catman, just better for this stage.
*[[Megidora (Uber Rare Cat)|Megidora]]: Provides nice [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control]] for the Bun Buns.
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]]: [[Freeze|Freezes]] everything in her range for long enough for you to recover whatever you may need along with good DPS.
*[[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Shining Amaterasu:]] A super generalist that outranges most of the bosses and does [[Massive Damage]] to them, making her a good choice to bring on any growing stages to deal great damage.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Amazing tank for this stage. Can absorb countless hits from Bun Bun due to her insane HP and Floating resistance.

